 ## Subtopics
+
+### [TetWeave Optimization Pipeline](3240-tetweave-optimization-pipeline.md)
+A differentiable optimization method that reconstructs a target 3D mesh from 2D multi-view images by optimizing 3D points, SDF values, and SH coefficients. It builds on this method by including the initial phase where point positions and tetrahedral topology are also updated. It is distinguished from sibling methods by its explicit use of tetrahedralization and marching tetrahedra for mesh extraction.
 
